# Precedence

Project rules override these; repository documentation (`/docs`, `README.md`, ADRs) overrides
both. Project conventions beat skill defaults. When no skill applies, say so rather than
inventing a process.

Machine-local specifics — Jira project keys, boards, documentation repositories, cluster names,
local checkouts and Sonar keys — live in `~/.cursor/local/`, unversioned (symlinked to
`~/.claude/local/`). Read the file a command or skill names (`work-repos.md` for `~/repos`); if
it is missing, ask rather than guess.

A question about a work project's domain — why it is built as it is, mappings, providers,
release flow, programme decisions — starts at the knowledge base `doc-repos.md` names: read its
`README.md` and follow the links before reading code or guessing.
